50,000 vectors of 256 dimensions: 51.2 MB as 32-bit floats

    M  index file  beyond vectors  per vector  rule M x 8  recall@10   build
    8      55.5 MB          4.3 MB        85 B        64 B        95%    5.1s
   16      58.6 MB          7.4 MB       148 B       128 B       100%    7.9s
   32      65.0 MB         13.8 MB       276 B       256 B       100%   10.7s

The file holds the vectors, the bottom layer's links, the sparse upper layers and a
label per vector, so the overhead runs somewhat above the rule of thumb — and it is a
fraction of the vectors themselves.
Going from M=16 to M=32 multiplied the overhead by 1.9 and bought no recall it could show.
